{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"clojure -M -e \\\"(require 'yin.vm 'clojure.repl) (clojure.repl/source yin.vm/same-content?) (let [a (* 1.0 ##NaN) b (* -1.0 ##NaN)] (prn (meta a) (meta b) (not= a a) (not= b b) (#'yin.vm/same-content? a b) (#'yin.vm/same-content? nil nil) (#'yin.vm/same-content? 1 1)))\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"Loading initial Timbre config from: :default\n(defn- same-content?\n  \"True when `a` and `b` have equal content, treating NaN leaves as equal,\n   and carry `=` metadata at every\n   depth, including inside metadata itself (a metadata value, or a metadata\n   map's own metadata, compares through `same-content?` too). `=` alone ignores\n   metadata.\n\n   NaN map keys and set elements inside data payloads are out of scope\n   and fail closed when lookup misses.\n\n   Scope boundary: the set branch assumes ordinary set semantics, at most one\n   element per `=`-equivalence class; a set built with a comparator that\n   admits several `=`-equal, metadata-distinct elements is out of scope, the\n   same class of pathological-input residual `dao.jing.md` documents for its\n   own encoder (pathological symbols, scalar metadata). That deferred case is\n   silent and order-dependent, not reliably fail-closed: which `=`-equal\n   element the lookup picks depends on traversal order, so a metadata\n   mismatch may throw or may be silently accepted.\"\n  [a b]\n  (and (= (meta a) (meta b))\n       (or (nil? (meta a)) (same-content? (meta a) (meta b)))\n       (cond (map? a) (and (map? b)\n                                 (= (count a) (count b))\n                                 (every? (fn [[k v]]\n                                           (and (contains? b k)\n                                                (let [[k' v'] (find b k)]\n                                                  (and (same-content? k k')\n                                                       (same-content? v v')))))\n                                         a))\n             (set? a) (and (set? b)\n                           (= (count a) (count b))\n                           (every? (fn [e]\n                                     (same-content? e (some #(when (= e %) %) b)))\n                                   a))\n             (sequential? a) (and (sequential? b)\n                                  (= (count a) (count b))\n                                  (every? true? (map same-content? a b)))\n             :else (or (= a b) (and (not= a a) (not= b b))))))\nnil nil true true false true true\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
